  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for PLWHAs in Mangabeira, Jo&#xe3;o Pessoa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Medical and Counselling Centre (CAMP) in Mangabeira was established as a grass roots, community health initiative by the Sisters of the Sacred Heart of Mary in 1993.  Initially the work focused on preventative health education and the promotion of alternative and herbal medicines. Counselling and training was also given to local women. Toward the end of the 1990s, there was a rapid growth of the number of cases of HIV in the area, and CAMP adapted to local demand and began to provide support and care services specifically for PLWHAs. CAFOD has been supporting CAMP since 1999.

CAMP seeks to contribute to the integral health of those living in poverty through the provision of medical, psychological and therapeutic services. CAMP promotes educational processes that encourage self-help and the recovery and the exercise of citizenship. A key feature of their work is to provide advice and support for PLWHAS, their families, poor communities and other organisations working with HIV and AIDS. This project focuses on:
- contributing to the integral health of the individual, through the provision of medical, psychological and therapeutic services;
- promoting educational processes that encourage self-help and the recovery and exercise of citizenship; 
- providing advice and support on STD and HIV &amp;AIDS for poor communities and other organisations working with HIV and AIDS.</narrative>
  </description>
